# component: sidebar
# decisions: A11Y-2, BRD-1, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-6, FRM-4
# hunks:
#   BRD-1: the floating variant's inner surface swaps upstream's
#     `group-data-[variant=floating]:ring-1 …:ring-sidebar-border` box-shadow outline for a real
#     `…:border …:border-sidebar-border` — the sidebar's own hairline ink, so the edge matches the
#     `sidebar` variant's `border-e`. The floating sidebar is a floating surface, and MK extended
#     BRD-1 to it on 23-09-2026. The container already budgets `+2px` for the collapsed width.
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: `outline-hidden` and `focus-visible:ring-2` are removed from all five controls
#     that carry them — `SidebarGroupLabel`, `SidebarGroupAction`, `SidebarMenuButton`,
#     `SidebarMenuAction` and `SidebarMenuSubButton`. `outline-hidden` is the v3 spelling of 'no
#     outline': upstream suppresses the browser's and paints its own 2px ring instead, and this
#     system does the opposite. `ring-sidebar-ring` is left in place on each — it is a colour
#     with no ring width behind it any more, it paints nothing, and removing it would take the
#     `--sidebar-ring` token's only reference with it.
#   FRM-4: `disabled:pointer-events-none` and `aria-disabled:pointer-events-none` are dropped
#     from `SidebarMenuButton` and `SidebarMenuSubButton`, so a disabled nav row stays hoverable
#     and a Tooltip can explain why. Both opacity halves stay.
#   A11Y-2: `md:after:hidden` is dropped from `SidebarMenuAction` and `SidebarGroupAction`.
#     Both are `w-5` (20px) squares, which is under the 24px floor, and upstream already solves
#     that the way A11Y-2 asks — with an invisible `after:absolute after:-inset-2` hit area — and
#     then switches the area OFF again at `md` and above. Measured with a real
#     `document.elementFromPoint` probe over compiled Tailwind: 36x36 with 0/5 obstruction misses
#     at 390px, and 20x20 at 1280px, i.e. 4px under the floor at EVERY desktop width. Nothing in
#     this repository could have seen it — the global geometry lane sweeps at 320px only, where
#     `md:` never applies. § 5.2 lists `sidebar` under A11Y-2 as a CANDIDATE to audit rather than
#     an assignment; this is that audit finding a real violation, so the exception is applied. The
#     hit area is the only thing that changes: the visible 20px box, its position and its hover
#     wash are upstream's. `sidebar.test.tsx` measures both controls at both widths.
#   registry layout (DOC-1): `@/hooks/use-mobile` becomes `@/components/ui/use-mobile`. Hooks are
#     `registry:hook` items alongside the components in this registry, which is the path the
#     three-copy model and `shadcn add @vegastack/use-mobile` both use.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
